where and δ x i {\displaystyle \delta _{x_{i}}} {\displaystyle \delta _{x_{i}}} is the Dirac measure , and the quality function is just L2 loss: d ( x , x ′ ) = ‖ x − x ′ ‖ 2 2 {\displaystyle d(x,x')=\|x-x'\|_{2}^{2}} {\displaystyle d(x,x')=\|x-x'\|_{2}^{2}} , ‖ ⋅ ‖ 2 {\displaystyle \|\cdot \|_{2}} {\displaystyle \|\cdot \|_{2}} is the Euclidean norm. Then the problem of searching for the optimal autoencoder is just a least-squares optimization:
